    "reason": "The assertion claims that offline inference reduces GPU hours for regression/classification tasks. This is factually unsound as a general rule because 'offline' implies batch processing, which often requires loading entire datasets into memory or using larger models to maintain accuracy, whereas streaming (online) inference allows early termination and lower memory footprints, potentially reducing compute per sample in specific scenarios. The validation failure correctly identifies that resource constraints (memory limits) can negate the claimed reduction; thus, the assertion lacks necessary qualifiers regarding dataset size, memory availability, and model architecture. Without explicit conditions guaranteeing the reduction holds across all physical configurations, the claim is uncertain/false.",
